%% D6. Diagnostics and interpretation workflow
%% A guide to reasoning, not an automatic rule for choosing a model.
flowchart TD
  A["Fitted model"] --> B{"Warnings: convergence, singular fit, separation?"}
  B -->|Yes| B1["Investigate: rescale time and covariates, check gradients, compare optimisers, simplify random effects for a stated reason (Module 11)"]
  B1 --> A
  B -->|No| C["Residuals: against fitted values and time, by group; Q-Q plots; DHARMa for GLMMs"]
  C --> D["Random effects: BLUP plots (read with care) and comparison of covariance models"]
  D --> E["Influence: leave-one-subject-out change in the key estimate"]
  E --> F{"Do any problems matter for the estimand?"}
  F -->|Yes| G["Revise for substantive reasons, record the change in the analysis log, report both if the primary model was prespecified"]
  F -->|No| H["Interpret on the scale of the question: EMMs, differences in mean change, probabilities, rates"]
  G --> H
  H --> I["Report estimates with CIs, the model, its assumptions, missing-data handling and sensitivity analyses (Module 12)"]
  classDef q fill:#ffffff,stroke:#555555,color:#222222;
  classDef m fill:#eef4f8,stroke:#0b5d8f,color:#222222;
  class A,B,F q;
  class B1,C,D,E,G,H,I m;
